  "notes": "Piano-and-guitar confessional pop on a 1990s alt-rock chassis, straight 2&4 against a half-time parent. The drum grammar is the entry's most specific claim and it is authored literally: \"ballads open drumless, then a kick + syncopated handclap pattern with the clap displaced off the backbeat\", so the snare stack is `clap` alone with a real `layerClapOffsetMs` spread and `offGridMs` pushing the backbeat late, and \"the documented device is switching the kick to double-time for the second verse\" is the wide `densityPerBar` range plus `fourOnFloorInChorus`. \"Rock mode is a live kit with crash-heavy chorus accents and no hat filigree\" is the low `fillDensity` and the `crash` perc lane. Harmony is \"close-position triads with pedal-tone left hand\" and \"loops are 4 bars\", so `triad` sits high and `chordDurationBeats` is a 4-bar frame; \"ballads favour major keys with borrowed minor iv for the pre-chorus lift\" is the `borrowed` map, which swaps a IV for a iv rather than writing a second family. Melody register is the documented \"drivers license\" span G3—F5 written in the low-middle; \"conversational and low in verses, then leaps to a sustained belt/near-shout at the chorus peak\" is the `octaveJumpProb` ceiling and the arch contour. Backing vocals are \"stacked in unison-plus-octave\", so the counter is `octave_echo`. There is no `bass808` block — the entry says \"no 808 lane; synth or electric bass entering late as the lift event\" — and the low `anticipationProb` is that lateness. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize pair and `bpm.mode` 92 (the research gives ballads 78—105 and pop-rock 124—140, so the mode is the midpoint of the first-named core band). ⚠ The research's own fast-mode half-time reading is marked [LOW-CONF] there and is not encoded here.",
